Ultralytics (AGPL-3.0) — AFFECTS pipeline/detect_car.py
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  pipeline/detect_car.py imports `ultralytics` and loads the `yolo11m.pt`
  weights. Both the package and the weights are licensed AGPL-3.0.

  Ultralytics' stated position is that building on their package requires
  releasing your work under AGPL-3.0 or obtaining an Ultralytics Enterprise
  Licence. Whether a script that merely imports the library constitutes a
  derivative work is not settled, and this project does not redistribute
  ultralytics.

  Practical consequence: the Apache-2.0 licence on this repository should NOT
  be read as permission to use pipeline/detect_car.py, or a work derived from
  it, in a closed-source product. Anyone doing so must satisfy AGPL-3.0
  themselves, or replace the detector.

  pipeline/reframe_src.py consumes detections as JSON and does not import
  ultralytics, so the reframing solver is unaffected and a different detector
  can be substituted at that boundary.

  https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics

